# Test models are not carried in the repository. They are large (430 MiB of glb at the
# point this was written, one export alone over GitHub's 100 MiB per-file limit) and most
# of them — trex, totoro, lotus, water, box — are scratch, not content.
#
# The scene does load several of these, so a fresh clone cannot run scripts/smoke.sh or
# scripts/verify-parity.sh until they are put back by hand. .gitattributes already routes
# binary assets to LFS if any of this is ever tracked again.
assets/Models/

# The circuit and the engine bank, for the same reason and with the same consequence. The Bathurst
# exports are 251 MiB (visual), 30 MiB (the superseded collision export) and 15 MiB (physics), and
# the first of those is over GitHub's 100 MiB per-file hard limit on its own; the FMOD bank is a
# 57 MiB binary. All four are generated by ~/dev/ac-car-data from Assetto Corsa content, so they are
# reproducible rather than authored here.
#
# As with assets/Models/ above: a fresh clone cannot run scripts/smoke.sh or
# scripts/verify-parity.sh until these are put back by hand.
assets/Tracks/*.glb
assets/Sfx/

# The navigation mesh bake beside the traffic export: 33 MB of derived numbers, regenerated by
# ~/dev/ac-car-data's navmesh.py from the track and collider exports above, and put back by hand
# like them. (The traffic export itself is tracked, being half a megabyte.)
assets/Tracks/*/grand_city_parkway_navmesh.json
assets/Tracks/*/*_navmesh.json
